WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:04.770
I'm Jenna Fisher.

2
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.090
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

3
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.370
We were on The Office together.

4
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:08.610
And we're best friends.

5
00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:12.430
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.

6
00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:16.790
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes

7
00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:19.410
stories that only two people who were there can tell you.

8
00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:20.570
We're The Office ladies.

9
00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:26.080
Hi, you guys.

10
00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:27.680
I hope you're having a great day.

11
00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.140
Today, we're going to talk about gossip.

12
00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:34.220
It is the season premiere of season six.

13
00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:36.800
Holy moly, we're at season six.

14
00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:37.300
Yeah.

15
00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:40.500
We're going down the other side of the mountain.

16
00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.940
We hit the peak at 100 episodes.

17
00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:43.960
Now we've got 104.

18
00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:44.760
Downhill all the way.

19
00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:47.580
No, that's not how I meant that metaphor to be.

20
00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.900
I just meant we're halfway to our destination.

21
00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:52.980
We're halfway there.

22
00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.560
Oh, no.

23
00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:57.440
Oh, now I heard it.

24
00:00:57.800 --> 00:00:59.120
Ooga, ooga, ooga, ooga.

25
00:00:59.240 --> 00:00:59.420
No?

26
00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:00.440
Okay, I'm going to stop.

27
00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:01.340
Oh, I'm liking this.

28
00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:07.100
Listen, this episode was written by Paul Lieberstein and directed by Paul Lieberstein.

29
00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.600
And here is your summary.

30
00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:16.140
When Michael regretfully reveals that Stanley is having an affair, he sets out to cover

31
00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:20.700
his tracks by spreading a bunch of lies about basically everyone in the office.

32
00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:26.860
But what he doesn't realize is that one of his lies turns out to be true.

33
00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:33.620
Before we get started on the fast facts, Angela, we have some gossip or maybe it's not gossip.

34
00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:34.540
Maybe it's true.

35
00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:36.400
Maybe it's the one true thing.

36
00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:37.280
Okay.

37
00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:38.340
It's totally real.

38
00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:39.320
It's not gossip.

39
00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:44.340
Guys, our book cover for office BFFs is out.

40
00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:45.160
It is out.

41
00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:45.820
It's official.

42
00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:46.600
Right now.

43
00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:47.520
You can see it.

44
00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:48.600
It's so cute.

45
00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:49.360
Can I say that?

46
00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:50.600
I can say it's cute, right?

47
00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:52.380
I mean, I hope we think it's cute.

48
00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:53.080
We picked it.

49
00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:53.680
We picked it.

50
00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:55.680
You guys, I think you know this about me by now.

51
00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:56.980
I love a photo booth.

52
00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:57.760
This is true.

53
00:01:57.980 --> 00:02:01.020
If I walk by a photo booth with you, you're going in it with me.

54
00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:04.440
And Jenna and I went into a photo booth at the mall one day.

55
00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:05.680
This was years ago.

56
00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:06.600
Years ago.

57
00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:07.380
Ten years ago, maybe?

58
00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:09.700
Was it more than that?

59
00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:10.500
Maybe more.

60
00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:14.320
I saved the photo strip from this mall photo booth.

61
00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:17.580
It's been on my bulletin board for a number of years.

62
00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:19.720
And it's the photo of our book cover.

63
00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:25.180
I'm realizing now that we chose a 15-year-old photo for our book cover,

64
00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:27.920
probably because we didn't want to pose for a photo.

65
00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:33.240
But actually, the point of it was to show the depth of our friendship,

66
00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:34.460
the length of our friendship,

67
00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:39.980
because so much of the book is going over the growth and history of our friendship.

68
00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:41.140
It is, you guys.

69
00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:44.100
It is our life through the office and beyond.

70
00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:48.440
Beyond Best Friendship Journal with the backdrop of this amazing show.

71
00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:54.000
And just a lot of our stories that we can't get into as much in the podcast are in the book.

72
00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:58.720
Also in the book are 400 of our personal photos.

73
00:02:59.000 --> 00:02:59.980
Can I just take a minute?

74
00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:00.660
400.

75
00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:04.240
That was so hard to narrow down because we had like 2,000.

76
00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:08.160
And they were like, you guys, your book cannot have 2,000 pictures.

77
00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:10.920
They told us we had to narrow it down to like 200.

78
00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:12.640
Jenna and I were like, we got it to 400.

79
00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:13.140
Yeah.

80
00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:14.240
Can we call it even?

81
00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:19.600
So these are truly our personal photos taken on our personal cameras,

82
00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:23.140
even back then when you had the old-timey cameras with film.

83
00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:25.780
Yes, and you had to go to the mall to the kiosk.

84
00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:26.080
Yep.

85
00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:26.540
Yeah.

86
00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:29.160
Those pictures all the way back to the pilot.

87
00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:29.980
Yeah.

88
00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:31.040
Of the office.

89
00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:34.060
The book is available for pre-order now.

90
00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:39.520
We would appreciate it if you pre-order it because it makes us look really good to our publishers.

91
00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:46.020
I wish you could see Jenna's face right now because she's doing that really cute face that your kids do when they really want something at Christmas.

92
00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:48.940
So yeah, pre-order would be amazing.

93
00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:50.080
Thank you in advance.

94
00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:55.540
I know the Midwesterner in me gets very shy asking people to do things like that.

95
00:03:55.780 --> 00:04:00.040
But you can find a link to order the book on officeladies.com.

96
00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:03.820
We will, of course, put it on all of our social media platforms as well.

97
00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:04.260
Yes.

98
00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:05.700
So check out the cover.

99
00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:07.240
Office BFFs.

100
00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:08.040
Check it out.

101
00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:09.880
We can't wait to share this book with you.

102
00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:15.980
We're super excited to take it out in the world and meet you all and sign copies and do the whole shebang.

103
00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:17.680
And I will wear a fake flower.

104
00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:18.780
You mark my words.

105
00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:20.820
I don't doubt it for a second.

106
00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:22.600
Should we get back to the episode?

107
00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:23.680
Let's do it.

108
00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:30.000
Fast fact number one, Gossip, as I said, was our season six premiere episode.

109
00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:37.820
It aired on September 17th, 2009, and it was seen by 8.21 million viewers.

110
00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:38.540
Wow.

111
00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:39.820
That seems like a lot.

112
00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:41.360
It was a lot.

113
00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:48.880
However, our viewership was down 18% compared to the season five premiere of Weight Loss.

114
00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:49.320
Ooh.

115
00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:53.580
So I guess we took a little dip here with our premiere episode.

116
00:04:53.800 --> 00:05:02.940
But The Office was still the leading comedy on NBC at the time, and we were sort of the anchor for the other shows.

117
00:05:03.140 --> 00:05:05.280
I found an old promo.

118
00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:07.380
Oh, I love an old promo.

119
00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:14.920
That was kicking off the whole, like, fall season, and The Office was very prominent in it.

120
00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:16.020
Will you guys play it?

121
00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:19.040
Here's why summer being over is a good thing.

122
00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:19.320
Yeah!

123
00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:22.160
Because now we get new comedy on NBC Thursday.

124
00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:23.180
That's cool.

125
00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:25.920
We'll finally confirm the big baby news on The Office.

126
00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:26.960
She peed out a stick.

127
00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:27.620
I did.

128
00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:29.300
But it was inconclusive.

129
00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:37.140
And we welcome back Parks and Rec, 30 Rock, and SNL in primetime, plus the new comedy Community, a perfect fit on Thursdays.

130
00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:37.840
You ready, Amiga?

131
00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:38.820
Let's see.

132
00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:40.160
And it always ends with J.

133
00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:46.480
All your favorite comedies are back on One Great Night, Thursday, September 17th on NBC.

134
00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:48.400
Oh, man.

135
00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:50.020
I miss those promo guys.

136
00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:52.760
Those guys, they crack me up every time.

137
00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:55.360
They're like, all your favorites in one place.

138
00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:55.920
Yeah.

139
00:05:56.140 --> 00:05:57.840
They kind of do a breathy thing.

140
00:05:57.840 --> 00:06:01.180
Well, when I saw this promo, it made me think of something.

141
00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:01.700
What?

142
00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:03.940
Well, they say, summer is over.

143
00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:04.900
You know, we're back.

144
00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:05.400
Yeah, yeah.

145
00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:10.540
Why did the documentary film crew stop filming us every summer?

146
00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:13.200
There's always a time jump.

147
00:06:13.340 --> 00:06:15.440
Lady, because they're a fakie film crew.

148
00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:18.600
I mean, why not film us in the summer?

149
00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:20.300
We jump ahead in time.

150
00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:24.320
It's been several weeks since Pam and Jim got their pregnancy news.

151
00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:28.300
And now, you know, she's quite far along by this episode.

152
00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:29.860
I just, I'm like, why?

153
00:06:30.020 --> 00:06:31.880
Why did they, why did they take a break?

154
00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:34.080
All right.

155
00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:35.540
Fast fact number two.

156
00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:41.160
Gossip was the first episode to feature Ellie Kemper as a full cast member.

157
00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:49.600
It was also the first episode of The Office to air since the release of The Hangover, starring our very own Ed HelMs.

158
00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:53.720
This movie was a huge hit.

159
00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:54.000
Yeah.

160
00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:54.660
Huge.

161
00:06:55.520 --> 00:07:01.660
If you don't know it, it's the story of these three guys who go to Vegas for a bachelor party, but they lose the groom.

162
00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:06.060
And they wake up from this night of intense partying.

163
00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:10.800
The groom is gone, and they have to retrace their steps and try to find him.

164
00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:12.500
And Ed was one of the stars.

165
00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:18.820
This movie made $469 million at the box office.

166
00:07:18.940 --> 00:07:20.180
What the heck?

167
00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:26.120
Bradley Cooper, Zach Galifianakis, Ed Helms became superstars.

168
00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:28.920
Ken Jeong was in this movie, Superstar.

169
00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:36.400
I went to the Hangover DVD release party in Las Vegas with Rachel Harris.

170
00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:37.200
You didn't.

171
00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:37.660
I did.

172
00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:39.860
Because Rachel Harris was in the movie.

173
00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:40.440
Yes.

174
00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:44.020
She played Ed's girlfriend, the sort of persnickety girlfriend.

175
00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:45.780
I witnessed her plus one.

176
00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:48.980
And lady, guess where this big party was in Vegas?

177
00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:51.160
Um, I don't know.

178
00:07:51.660 --> 00:07:52.600
Caesar's Palace.

179
00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:54.400
Oh, of course, because the movie.

180
00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:57.900
Club Pure, I found some red carpet photos.

181
00:07:57.900 --> 00:07:59.040
No, you did not.

182
00:07:59.320 --> 00:07:59.880
From this evening.

183
00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:02.300
And I cannot wait to show them to you.

184
00:08:03.260 --> 00:08:03.740
Who?

185
00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:06.520
Angela!

186
00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:09.800
Angela has on boots that go up to her knees.

187
00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:11.580
Black leather go-go boots.

188
00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:12.580
Oh, wow.

189
00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:14.080
Look at you.

190
00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:15.380
I was in Vegas.

191
00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:18.200
You gotta, like, bring out your boots for Vegas.

192
00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:21.780
So, yeah, I went to the Hangover DVD release party.

193
00:08:21.780 --> 00:08:27.960
Well, we want you guys to know that Ed was a horrible person after he became a big star.

194
00:08:28.380 --> 00:08:29.620
No, he wasn't.

195
00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:32.300
He was just even more Ed.

196
00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:33.680
He never changed.

197
00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:35.500
What a sweet guy.

198
00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:37.880
We were so happy for this big success.

199
00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:38.600
Yeah.

200
00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:43.160
He went on to make more Hangover movies and more movies.

201
00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:44.600
And develop TV series.

202
00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:46.080
But he's still the same old Ed.

203
00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:46.760
He is.

204
00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:51.680
Fast fact number three, I have titled, What Did You Do Over That Summer?

205
00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:52.640
Hmm.

206
00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:56.620
Because I was like, this was like a life-altering summer for Ed HelMs.

207
00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:56.920
Yeah.

208
00:08:56.920 --> 00:09:01.320
It was a life-altering summer for Ellie Kemper because she was made a regular on this TV show.

209
00:09:01.740 --> 00:09:05.580
I realized I had a life-altering summer as well.

210
00:09:05.740 --> 00:09:06.300
What'd you do?

211
00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:09.480
Two very big things happened to me over this summer.

212
00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:15.460
The first thing that happened was that my beloved Andi cat, you know, the one that was

213
00:09:15.460 --> 00:09:17.320
in the People magazine shoot with me.

214
00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:19.020
The one that you had a voice for.

215
00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:20.320
You would talk as Andi.

216
00:09:20.460 --> 00:09:21.140
Yes, I would.

217
00:09:21.280 --> 00:09:22.780
We haven't shared about that.

218
00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:23.480
Oh, sorry.

219
00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:24.080
We haven't.

220
00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:25.860
That's okay.

221
00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:30.540
Everyone who knows me going all the way back to college knows I had a little voice for Andi.

222
00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:32.920
I'll have you know Sunny has one as well.

223
00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:33.560
Oh, yeah.

224
00:09:33.740 --> 00:09:37.320
All of your animals have their own unique accents.

225
00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:38.020
They do.

226
00:09:38.260 --> 00:09:43.620
Because by the way, I think Andi's name was Andi, but he pronounced it Andi.

227
00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:44.140
Andi, yeah.

228
00:09:44.260 --> 00:09:45.200
That was a choice he made.

229
00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:45.580
Right.

230
00:09:45.780 --> 00:09:50.300
So anyway, sweet Andi passed away over this summer.

231
00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:55.180
He was almost 17 years old, but that was a big thing for me because he had traveled with

232
00:09:55.180 --> 00:10:01.020
me all the way from Kirksville, Missouri, all the way to Hollywood, and he was my love.

233
00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:01.560
I know.

234
00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:02.280
Really and truly.

235
00:10:02.900 --> 00:10:08.300
So also that summer, though, Angela, Lee proposed to me.

236
00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:09.500
Oh, my gosh.

237
00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:10.200
That's right.

238
00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:10.900
Yes.

239
00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:13.080
We were in Paris.

240
00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:14.280
Oh, Paris.

241
00:10:14.520 --> 00:10:15.220
Paris, Paris.

242
00:10:15.580 --> 00:10:18.120
And he proposed by the river.

243
00:10:18.460 --> 00:10:21.060
We were having a little picnic with wine and cheese.

244
00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:21.320
What the heck?

245
00:10:21.500 --> 00:10:22.240
We were so Parisian.

246
00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:23.400
Is this a rom-com?

247
00:10:24.460 --> 00:10:31.760
Well, then it got even more rom-com because Lee and I were like, oh, maybe we keep the

248
00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:33.960
engagement to ourselves for a little while.

249
00:10:34.220 --> 00:10:36.080
I mean, we told all of our close friends.

250
00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:37.100
We told our family.

251
00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:41.940
But we thought, like, maybe we don't go public with the news for a while.

252
00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:42.700
I don't know.

253
00:10:42.840 --> 00:10:43.260
Yeah, yeah.

254
00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:45.120
Just keeping things private.

255
00:10:45.820 --> 00:10:52.420
Well, someone in this little Parisian restaurant overheard us telling another couple that we

256
00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:53.320
had gotten engaged.

257
00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:57.020
So while we're flying back home, it hit the news.

258
00:10:57.240 --> 00:10:58.980
I mean, talk about gossip.

259
00:10:59.160 --> 00:10:59.600
Oh, my gosh.

260
00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:00.660
This is so on theme.

261
