Because I remember seeing this whiteboard in season three.

936
00:43:01.940 --> 00:43:03.000
Andy is at the top.

937
00:43:03.440 --> 00:43:06.740
And I don't think I've seen this change in years.

938
00:43:07.060 --> 00:43:12.500
Well, to be fair, we were rarely over in that corner, so it might have gotten overlooked.

939
00:43:13.340 --> 00:43:16.320
Michael is determined to keep spreading this information.

940
00:43:16.660 --> 00:43:19.480
He is now trying to get Kevin to guess.

941
00:43:20.220 --> 00:43:24.000
Yes, he's playing that word guessing game, Hangman.

942
00:43:24.300 --> 00:43:24.440
Yeah.

943
00:43:24.980 --> 00:43:25.960
Kevin's not getting it.

944
00:43:26.000 --> 00:43:27.040
No, Kevin's not getting it.

945
00:43:27.040 --> 00:43:32.480
So, lady, this reminded me of Wheel of Fortune.

946
00:43:32.860 --> 00:43:33.480
Oh, yeah.

947
00:43:33.480 --> 00:43:35.380
Because Wheel of Fortune is based on this game.

948
00:43:35.600 --> 00:43:36.200
Oh, yeah?

949
00:43:36.440 --> 00:43:37.180
You guess a phrase.

950
00:43:37.580 --> 00:43:41.260
My family was obsessed with Wheel of Fortune.

951
00:43:41.880 --> 00:43:46.160
We had the home game, the Wheel of Fortune home game.

952
00:43:46.920 --> 00:43:51.300
And my mom, bless her heart, was a horrible guesser.

953
00:43:51.580 --> 00:43:52.500
Just horrible.

954
00:43:53.060 --> 00:43:54.620
Our favorite family example.

955
00:43:54.740 --> 00:43:58.480
You know when you have those things that happen in your family that go down as like your family lore?

956
00:43:58.640 --> 00:43:59.200
Sure, sure.

957
00:43:59.380 --> 00:43:59.620
Okay.

958
00:44:00.060 --> 00:44:02.020
We were playing this game.

959
00:44:02.200 --> 00:44:04.040
My mom's trying to guess the phrase.

960
00:44:04.960 --> 00:44:07.260
And she screams out of nowhere.

961
00:44:07.380 --> 00:44:08.140
I've got it!

962
00:44:08.360 --> 00:44:09.120
I've got it!

963
00:44:09.260 --> 00:44:10.120
Gold-toothed tiger!

964
00:44:10.240 --> 00:44:11.240
Gold-toothed tiger!

965
00:44:11.980 --> 00:44:15.220
We're like, Mom, gold-toothed tiger?

966
00:44:15.360 --> 00:44:19.160
What is this famous phrase, gold-toothed tiger?

967
00:44:19.720 --> 00:44:21.400
I don't remember what it was.

968
00:44:21.560 --> 00:44:23.140
It was not gold-toothed tiger.

969
00:44:23.380 --> 00:44:24.020
No, of course not.

970
00:44:24.820 --> 00:44:26.940
So, anyway, now that's like my sister.

971
00:44:26.940 --> 00:44:27.440
A catchphrase.

972
00:44:27.440 --> 00:44:29.880
Yeah, my sister and I can be like gold-toothed tiger, Mom.

973
00:44:30.400 --> 00:44:37.860
But my sister and I became obsessed, and we researched the most common letters in the English language.

974
00:44:38.120 --> 00:44:42.280
Wait, isn't one that you're always supposed to guess like S or T?

975
00:44:42.800 --> 00:44:43.800
T is one.

976
00:44:43.940 --> 00:44:44.420
Okay, T.

977
00:44:44.620 --> 00:44:45.260
I'll tell you.

978
00:44:45.360 --> 00:44:51.600
Here are the 12 most commonly occurring letters in the English language, from most to leaSt.

979
00:44:52.020 --> 00:44:52.700
E.

980
00:44:53.040 --> 00:44:53.720
Okay.

981
00:44:53.980 --> 00:44:54.240
T.

982
00:44:54.960 --> 00:44:55.580
A.

983
00:44:56.340 --> 00:44:57.020
O.

984
00:44:57.420 --> 00:44:58.100
I.

985
00:44:58.800 --> 00:44:59.480
N.

986
00:45:00.620 --> 00:45:05.360
S-H-R-D-L-U.

987
00:45:06.020 --> 00:45:10.100
So, if you're ever on Wheel of Fortune, and you're going to buy a vowel, buy an E.

988
00:45:10.360 --> 00:45:10.720
Okay.

989
00:45:11.000 --> 00:45:14.100
If you're going to guess a consonant, the first one you should guess is T.

990
00:45:14.220 --> 00:45:14.320
T.

991
00:45:14.520 --> 00:45:15.780
And the second one is N.

992
00:45:16.040 --> 00:45:21.040
I didn't know that, but I feel like some of it just mushed into my brain, because my grandmother

993
00:45:22.100 --> 00:45:24.720
faithfully watched Wheel of Fortune every single day.

994
00:45:25.140 --> 00:45:27.000
It was one of her favorite shows.

995
00:45:27.560 --> 00:45:28.940
She was so good.

996
00:45:29.400 --> 00:45:31.300
She could guess way before everyone else.

997
00:45:31.400 --> 00:45:33.760
We used to joke, grandmother, you've got to go on Wheel of Fortune.

998
00:45:33.880 --> 00:45:35.860
She's like, oh, no, I am not going to be on television.

999
00:45:36.660 --> 00:45:36.940
No.

1000
00:45:38.400 --> 00:45:41.360
And she loved Pat Sajak and Vanna White.

1001
00:45:41.500 --> 00:45:42.480
They could do no wrong.

1002
00:45:42.640 --> 00:45:42.900
Oh.

1003
00:45:43.120 --> 00:45:44.500
And she knew everything about them.

1004
00:45:44.760 --> 00:45:45.240
Yes.

1005
00:45:45.400 --> 00:45:45.780
Same.

1006
00:45:45.940 --> 00:45:47.000
My family was obsessed.

1007
00:45:47.320 --> 00:45:48.220
I love it.

1008
00:45:48.520 --> 00:45:53.600
Just to close this out, I can also tell you the most difficult words to guess.

1009
00:45:54.020 --> 00:45:54.780
Oh, really?

1010
00:45:55.000 --> 00:45:55.180
Yeah.

1011
00:45:55.180 --> 00:46:02.160
This was according to a 2010 study conducted by John McLoone for Wolfram Research.

1012
00:46:02.540 --> 00:46:02.900
Ooh.

1013
00:46:03.180 --> 00:46:07.760
Why Wolfram Research decided to conduct this survey, I don't know.

1014
00:46:07.900 --> 00:46:09.560
I don't know, but I appreciate it.

1015
00:46:09.560 --> 00:46:20.520
But the five most difficult words to guess in a word guessing game are jazz, buzz, two Zs,

1016
00:46:20.740 --> 00:46:23.960
haj, fizz, and fuzz.

1017
00:46:23.960 --> 00:46:26.280
Because people are not good at guessing Z words.

1018
00:46:26.520 --> 00:46:27.140
I guess not.

1019
00:46:27.580 --> 00:46:27.960
Yeah.

1020
00:46:28.280 --> 00:46:31.160
I guess you can use that information if you want.

1021
00:46:31.320 --> 00:46:31.520
Yeah.

1022
00:46:31.720 --> 00:46:36.740
If it will not help you to guess E-T-A-N-S-H-R-D-L-U.

