Maybe once Michael put Dwight in charge of it, it actually got done.

1270
00:58:07.260 --> 00:58:07.660
Perhaps.

1271
00:58:08.300 --> 00:58:11.080
I love that Dwight gives them his business card.

1272
00:58:11.080 --> 00:58:12.720
He says, you can call me day or night.

1273
00:58:13.220 --> 00:58:16.200
And then one of the interns says, why would I call you at night?

1274
00:58:16.620 --> 00:58:17.100
Eric does.

1275
00:58:17.280 --> 00:58:17.400
Yeah.

1276
00:58:17.580 --> 00:58:19.680
And then he says, no, you can't call me at all.

1277
00:58:19.820 --> 00:58:20.880
And Jim's like, well.

1278
00:58:21.340 --> 00:58:23.580
Good luck next time you're stuck between a moose and a bear.

1279
00:58:23.940 --> 00:58:25.440
Between a moose and her cubs.

1280
00:58:25.620 --> 00:58:26.460
Oh, and her cubs.

1281
00:58:27.860 --> 00:58:32.140
Well, the rumors are coming out because people start commenting.

1282
00:58:32.360 --> 00:58:35.340
For example, Erin says to Kelly, I'm so happy you're eating again.

1283
00:58:36.100 --> 00:58:36.380
Yeah.

1284
00:58:36.780 --> 00:58:41.240
And then Andy congratulates Jim on little baby tuna.

1285
00:58:41.480 --> 00:58:42.440
Little Toro.

1286
00:58:42.960 --> 00:58:45.320
Jim pulls Pam aside and he's like, they know.

1287
00:58:45.320 --> 00:58:47.000
I don't know how they know, but they know.

1288
00:58:47.380 --> 00:58:51.800
This brings us to my favorite line of the show.

1289
00:58:52.180 --> 00:58:53.020
What is it?

1290
00:58:53.200 --> 00:58:53.600
Is it?

1291
00:58:53.700 --> 00:58:54.780
I know what it is.

1292
00:58:54.900 --> 00:58:59.680
When Creed says, someone is saying the rumor about Creed is that he has asthma.

1293
00:58:59.920 --> 00:59:00.180
Yeah.

1294
00:59:00.180 --> 00:59:02.420
And if that gets out, they're not going to let him scuba.

1295
00:59:02.920 --> 00:59:07.600
And he has a talking head where he says, if he can't scuba, then what has all of this

1296
00:59:07.600 --> 00:59:08.120
been about?

1297
00:59:08.500 --> 00:59:10.020
What has he been working toward?

1298
00:59:11.520 --> 00:59:12.900
I love it so much.

1299
00:59:13.060 --> 00:59:14.600
I love the scuba talking head.

1300
00:59:14.600 --> 00:59:18.960
I'm pretty sure I remember John breaking though, when Creed said, they won't let me scuba.

1301
00:59:20.060 --> 00:59:22.460
Just Creed saying the word scuba.

1302
00:59:24.100 --> 00:59:27.560
I would like to point out one thing in this scene.

1303
00:59:27.960 --> 00:59:29.720
Many of you probably didn't catch it.

1304
00:59:29.920 --> 00:59:34.160
Unless you've ever had a really horrible time growing out your bangs.

1305
00:59:34.900 --> 00:59:41.000
If you go to 15 minutes 07, you'll see my hair awkwardly trying to be a ponytail, but

1306
00:59:41.000 --> 00:59:47.260
it can't really be a ponytail because I decided to get bangs and it took forever to grow them

1307
00:59:47.260 --> 00:59:47.500
out.

1308
00:59:47.820 --> 00:59:49.500
Look at this sad ponytail.

1309
00:59:50.020 --> 00:59:54.960
I mean, I have to say that looks like Pam's hair from seasons one through three.

1310
00:59:55.820 --> 01:00:01.440
The little swoop that we used to do with my half bangs is what that reminds me of.

1311
01:00:01.600 --> 01:00:02.260
Oh, bangs.

1312
01:00:02.680 --> 01:00:07.040
Well, Oscar wants everyone to know he is not the voice of the Taco Bell dog.

1313
01:00:07.500 --> 01:00:08.820
Toby is not a virgin.

1314
01:00:09.480 --> 01:00:11.120
The conference room is abuzz.

1315
01:00:11.280 --> 01:00:13.500
Everyone is trading rumors about themselves.

1316
01:00:13.780 --> 01:00:17.520
Jim is like, guys, has everybody heard a crazy rumor about themselves today?

1317
01:00:18.060 --> 01:00:20.060
And Michael is like, you know what?

1318
01:00:20.120 --> 01:00:21.280
Let's just forget all of them.

1319
01:00:21.440 --> 01:00:23.040
Well, they start tracing it all back.

1320
01:00:23.220 --> 01:00:26.420
And guess where every rumor came from?

1321
01:00:26.720 --> 01:00:27.300
Mm-hmm.

1322
01:00:27.620 --> 01:00:28.120
Michael.

1323
01:00:28.420 --> 01:00:31.140
Who runs to the elevator because he knows.

1324
01:00:31.460 --> 01:00:35.320
But the entire gang stops him, confronts him.

1325
01:00:36.140 --> 01:00:40.820
Dwight cannot believe that he told people that Shroop Farms uses store-bought manure when Dwight

1326
01:00:40.820 --> 01:00:43.100
showed Michael where his manure comes from.

1327
01:00:43.260 --> 01:00:44.060
Oh, my gosh.

1328
01:00:44.700 --> 01:00:48.260
Eventually, Michael is going to admit that he started the rumors.

1329
01:00:48.620 --> 01:00:50.940
I actually love that Michael's like, hey, I'm a victim here, too.

1330
01:00:51.400 --> 01:00:53.460
I mean, people were saying I was a J.Crew model.

1331
01:00:54.240 --> 01:00:54.700
Exactly.

1332
01:00:55.040 --> 01:00:59.600
But Michael says he had to start all the rumors because one of the rumors is true.

1333
01:01:00.020 --> 01:01:01.840
He's not going to say which one.

1334
01:01:02.360 --> 01:01:04.120
He starts going around.

1335
01:01:04.440 --> 01:01:09.260
And Jim and Pam realize pretty quickly what the real rumor is.

1336
01:01:09.400 --> 01:01:09.760
Yeah.

1337
01:01:10.140 --> 01:01:11.600
That Stanley's having an affair.

1338
01:01:11.600 --> 01:01:15.380
But everyone's insisting that Michael say what the real rumor is.

1339
01:01:15.540 --> 01:01:17.200
And he's about to reveal that.

1340
01:01:17.520 --> 01:01:23.180
So Jim jumps in and says, the real thing is that Pam is pregnant.

1341
01:01:24.040 --> 01:01:26.520
And right away, Angela's like, I knew it.

1342
01:01:27.020 --> 01:01:27.700
I know.

1343
01:01:27.860 --> 01:01:32.020
And then Kevin is like, I knew it because Pam's boobs were bigger.

1344
01:01:32.680 --> 01:01:33.160
Boobs, boobs, boobs, boobs.

1345
01:01:33.720 --> 01:01:34.740
And Jim's like, okay, buddy.

1346
01:01:34.920 --> 01:01:35.120
Okay.

1347
01:01:35.860 --> 01:01:40.300
We had a fan question from Renata P from Rio de Janeiro, Brazil.

1348
01:01:41.140 --> 01:01:45.820
What are your thoughts about Jim's revelation to the whole office that the rumor about Pam

1349
01:01:45.820 --> 01:01:47.320
being pregnant was actually true?

1350
01:01:47.620 --> 01:01:51.380
I know he was trying to protect Stanley, and it never really bothered me before.

1351
01:01:51.540 --> 01:01:55.200
But in re-watching the scene yesterday, I was like, hey, maybe he should have had a

1352
01:01:55.200 --> 01:01:57.800
conversation with Pam before telling everyone.

1353
01:01:57.880 --> 01:01:58.980
What do we think?

1354
01:01:59.180 --> 01:02:02.660
I actually think Pam and Jim were on the same page in this moment because

1355
01:02:03.220 --> 01:02:08.620
the way Pam's body language was and your dialogue, it's like the two of you both knew,

1356
01:02:08.820 --> 01:02:09.260
oh, no.

1357
01:02:09.600 --> 01:02:10.340
Oh, no.

1358
01:02:10.520 --> 01:02:13.780
He's about to destroy Stanley's life.

1359
01:02:13.940 --> 01:02:14.260
Oh, no.

1360
01:02:14.340 --> 01:02:15.100
We've got to do something.

1361
01:02:15.240 --> 01:02:18.740
I felt like I saw that internal dialogue between the two of you.

1362
01:02:19.380 --> 01:02:23.140
Well, I'm glad to hear you say that, Angela, because that was our intention.

1363
01:02:23.440 --> 01:02:27.300
The intention was that Jim and Pam were going to both come to this realization.

1364
01:02:28.180 --> 01:02:30.700
And this is like they share a brain thing.

1365
01:02:30.700 --> 01:02:35.100
There are a couple and so it's a couple brain, couple brains.

1366
01:02:35.360 --> 01:02:37.400
So I totally get where Renata is coming from.

1367
01:02:37.900 --> 01:02:43.420
Our hope was that you would see Pam's permission in that moment.

1368
01:02:43.580 --> 01:02:45.180
Her participation in the moment.

1369
01:02:45.500 --> 01:02:49.000
And how we're sort of giving each other eye contact was our intention.

1370
01:02:49.280 --> 01:02:52.300
Of course, Michael, though, is like, no, no, no, that's not it.

1371
01:02:52.480 --> 01:02:55.620
And you guys are like, oh, will you stop it?

1372
01:02:55.680 --> 01:02:56.620
Like, just like, oh.

1373
01:02:56.620 --> 01:02:59.900
So she has to go out and get her sonogram photo.

1374
01:03:00.300 --> 01:03:05.640
One of my favorite things is when you go get your sonogram photo is that Kelly says,

1375
01:03:05.800 --> 01:03:07.160
well, are we just all going to wait here?

1376
01:03:07.320 --> 01:03:08.160
That was just Mindy.

1377
01:03:08.320 --> 01:03:09.680
That was just Mindy.

1378
01:03:10.540 --> 01:03:12.660
Well, we had a fan question from Ella R.

1379
01:03:12.740 --> 01:03:13.140
in England.

1380
01:03:13.160 --> 01:03:14.960
Is Pam's sonogram real?

1381
01:03:15.160 --> 01:03:16.580
And if not, how was it created?

1382
01:03:17.100 --> 01:03:17.980
Good question.

1383
01:03:18.540 --> 01:03:21.880
Our graphic artist, Ryan Cosgrove, he made this for us.

1384
01:03:21.880 --> 01:03:26.360
He repurposed an existing sonogram from his friend's wife.

1385
01:03:26.800 --> 01:03:27.040
Oh.

1386
01:03:27.360 --> 01:03:29.760
So somewhere out there, there's a little baby.

1387
01:03:30.000 --> 01:03:31.800
A little baby who got some screen time.

1388
01:03:32.080 --> 01:03:32.280
Yeah.

1389
01:03:33.020 --> 01:03:37.460
Well, when Pam presents her sonogram, Michael says, that's the inside of her vagina.

1390
01:03:37.820 --> 01:03:38.020
Yeah.

1391
01:03:38.180 --> 01:03:40.100
That's a picture of the inside of her vagina.

1392
01:03:40.700 --> 01:03:45.140
Very quickly, Jim and Pam talking head where they're like, uh-huh, now it's clear.

1393
01:03:45.300 --> 01:03:47.380
It's clear why we didn't want to tell these people.

1394
01:03:47.620 --> 01:03:51.020
Well, now Jim and Pam are going to be like in the principal's office.

1395
01:03:51.600 --> 01:03:55.820
Michael is devastated that they did not tell him first, that they did not tell him sooner.

1396
01:03:56.280 --> 01:03:58.380
They only just told their parents.

1397
01:03:58.800 --> 01:04:01.920
In the shooting draft, the line read like this.

1398
01:04:02.460 --> 01:04:04.100
Did you piss on a stick?

1399
01:04:05.940 --> 01:04:08.460
And I guess on the day they changed it to P.

1400
01:04:08.860 --> 01:04:11.940
But when I read that in the shooting draft, it was so jarring.

1401
01:04:12.080 --> 01:04:14.960
I'm like, why would he say, did you piss on a stick?

1402
01:04:15.680 --> 01:04:18.420
Well, Michael has done something, guys.

1403
01:04:18.420 --> 01:04:22.120
Anyways, he has called Stanley's wife.

1404
01:04:22.700 --> 01:04:24.900
This scene is so brilliant.

1405
01:04:25.680 --> 01:04:31.840
When Aaron says, Terry Hudson's on the line, you guys, your faces are like, you called her?

1406
01:04:32.020 --> 01:04:33.320
And Michael's like, I got this.

1407
01:04:33.420 --> 01:04:34.040
I can do it.

1408
01:04:34.200 --> 01:04:36.220
I'll tell her I'm redecorating my condo.

1409
01:04:36.300 --> 01:04:38.080
And they're like, no, Michael, don't.

1410
01:04:38.140 --> 01:04:39.160
You guys are like, don't.

1411
01:04:39.580 --> 01:04:39.980
Don't.

1412
01:04:39.980 --> 01:04:41.180
But he has this whole thing.

1413
01:04:41.340 --> 01:04:44.880
It's going to have to play out over months where he's redecorating the condo.

1414
01:04:44.980 --> 01:04:48.060
They're going to get quotes, but then they're going to get an argument about the cost of

1415
01:04:48.060 --> 01:04:48.240
things.

1416
01:04:48.360 --> 01:04:50.480
And eventually he's just going to have to call it all off.

1417
01:04:50.660 --> 01:04:53.960
And he literally is like, I've got this.

1418
01:04:54.260 --> 01:04:56.560
And Pam is like, Michael, please don't.

1419
01:04:56.720 --> 01:05:00.100
Michael picks up the phone and says, hey, what up, Cynthia?

1420
01:05:00.100 --> 01:05:04.440
Cynthia, I mean, just amazing.

1421
01:05:04.820 --> 01:05:07.920
Jim starts to walk over and Michael is waving him off like, I got it.

1422
01:05:07.980 --> 01:05:08.420
I got it.

1423
01:05:08.520 --> 01:05:10.680
And then he goes, hold on a second, Cynthia.

1424
01:05:11.460 --> 01:05:13.620
And then Jim just hangs up the phone.

1425
01:05:14.720 --> 01:05:16.940
We had a fan question from Kelsey S.

1426
01:05:17.080 --> 01:05:20.500
from Chandler, Arizona, who says, this is my absolute

1427
01:05:20.500 --> 01:05:22.260
favorite episode of all time.

1428
01:05:22.280 --> 01:05:24.000
This is my comfort episode.

1429
01:05:24.220 --> 01:05:25.740
I watch it all of the time.

1430
01:05:25.740 --> 01:05:30.640
And I need to know if the scene where Michael answers the call from Terry, was it all improvised

1431
01:05:30.640 --> 01:05:31.720
or was it scripted?

1432
01:05:32.380 --> 01:05:36.680
Everything from Steve's reaction to his hand movements on the phone is hilarious.

1433
01:05:36.680 --> 01:05:37.700
And I love it.

1434
01:05:38.480 --> 01:05:42.220
This entire scene played out exactly as scripted.

1435
01:05:42.460 --> 01:05:43.560
Minus the piss.

1436
01:05:43.800 --> 01:05:44.720
Minus the piss.

1437
01:05:44.960 --> 01:05:46.540
That's the only thing that changed.

1438
01:05:46.880 --> 01:05:48.260
It is 100% on the page.

1439
01:05:48.880 --> 01:05:49.780
Guess what?

1440
01:05:50.240 --> 01:05:53.760
Terry was already suspicious about this affair.

1441
01:05:53.760 --> 01:05:57.300
And this, I guess, proves it.

1442
01:05:58.140 --> 01:06:00.940
Stanley is going to vandalize Michael's car.

1443
01:06:01.320 --> 01:06:06.900
Stanley takes a crowbar to Michael's car and destroys it.

1444
01:06:07.060 --> 01:06:09.860
We had a couple of fan questions about this.

1445
01:06:10.320 --> 01:06:11.940
One from Rohit R.

1446
01:06:12.160 --> 01:06:12.880
in Norman, Oklahoma.

1447
01:06:12.880 --> 01:06:17.120
How much did the scene of Stanley smashing Michael's car cost?

1448
01:06:18.260 --> 01:06:19.480
And Monica F.

1449
01:06:19.680 --> 01:06:20.940
from North Carolina said,

1450
01:06:21.600 --> 01:06:26.980
It's so funny to me that Stanley had enough time to put on his sunglasses before smashing Michael's car.

1451
01:06:27.640 --> 01:06:30.960
Well, guys, Leslie did this smashing.

1452
01:06:31.280 --> 01:06:33.000
Randy said he had a very good time.

1453
01:06:33.160 --> 01:06:33.980
I would, too.

1454
01:06:34.140 --> 01:06:35.080
I would, too.

1455
01:06:35.440 --> 01:06:39.920
He said that they had to establish him wearing the sunglasses earlier in the episode

1456
01:06:39.920 --> 01:06:45.260
so that during this scene, he would have eye protection in case anything flew up in his eyes.

1457
01:06:46.060 --> 01:06:49.500
Randy said he smashed the heck out of that car.

1458
01:06:49.780 --> 01:06:50.780
It was a one-er.

1459
01:06:51.240 --> 01:06:52.000
Just one take.

1460
01:06:52.280 --> 01:06:55.160
It cost over $4,000 to repair.

1461
01:06:55.520 --> 01:06:56.920
I don't doubt it.

1462
01:06:57.000 --> 01:06:59.760
When he called up and started to mess with the convertible top?

1463
01:07:00.020 --> 01:07:00.280
Yeah.

1464
01:07:00.520 --> 01:07:02.040
I was like, oh, no.

1465
01:07:02.340 --> 01:07:02.820
Mm-hmm.

1466
01:07:02.820 --> 01:07:03.920
That's some cha-ching.

1467
01:07:04.720 --> 01:07:07.200
Well, guys, that's basically the end of this episode.

1468
01:07:07.340 --> 01:07:10.420
The interns have a little talking head at the end

1469
01:07:10.420 --> 01:07:15.120
where we find out that Michael just called them Jet Li, Julia Stiles, and Alan Thicke.

1470
01:07:15.220 --> 01:07:19.960
And that Eric never really learned how many pieces of paper were in a ream of paper.

1471
01:07:21.940 --> 01:07:25.480
In the very end credits at 21 minutes, 34 seconds,

1472
01:07:25.700 --> 01:07:28.580
Randy Cordray pointed something out to us, and I want to share it to you.

1473
01:07:28.580 --> 01:07:34.220
We see the name of our new unit production manager for season six, Steve Burgess.

1474
01:07:34.720 --> 01:07:42.200
Steve was a very old and dear friend of Randy, and I loved Steve Burgess so much.

1475
01:07:42.200 --> 01:07:45.360
He went on to be our line producer in the last seasons.

1476
01:07:45.600 --> 01:07:49.180
We adore him, and it was so fun to finally see his name.

1477
01:07:49.360 --> 01:07:54.060
Randy said when he brought him on board that Steve's contributions behind the scenes were immeasurable.

1478
01:07:54.380 --> 01:07:56.800
Yes, and we are still in touch with Steve today.

1479
01:07:56.800 --> 01:08:01.560
So when we get to those episodes where he was the line producer, we're going to get to hear from him.

1480
01:08:02.020 --> 01:08:02.100
Yay!

1481
01:08:03.420 --> 01:08:05.460
Ah, well, that's gossip.

1482
01:08:05.900 --> 01:08:11.100
Do you think I'll end up in the gossip magazines because of my soup dreams with Brad Pitt?

1483
01:08:11.360 --> 01:08:12.800
Would that be so weird?

1484
01:08:12.980 --> 01:08:15.060
That would be such a full circle moment.

1485
01:08:15.320 --> 01:08:15.800
I know.

1486
01:08:15.980 --> 01:08:17.220
Who's going to write about it?

1487
01:08:17.320 --> 01:08:18.040
I don't know.

1488
01:08:18.460 --> 01:08:19.440
Maybe no one.

1489
01:08:19.520 --> 01:08:20.900
No one cares about my soup.

1490
01:08:21.080 --> 01:08:22.000
Your fake soup?

1491
01:08:22.660 --> 01:08:23.940
My fake soup!

1492
01:08:23.960 --> 01:08:25.140
With Brad Pitt!

1493
01:08:27.060 --> 01:08:32.580
Listen, if we ever hear from Brad Pitt about the fake soup, I will be so excited.

1494
01:08:32.800 --> 01:08:34.180
If we ever hear from...

1495
01:08:34.180 --> 01:08:34.500
What?

1496
01:08:34.700 --> 01:08:34.920
What?

1497
01:08:34.920 --> 01:08:35.540
Oh, my gosh!

1498
01:08:36.320 --> 01:08:37.980
What if one day...

1499
01:08:37.980 --> 01:08:39.140
You scared the crap out of me!

1500
01:08:39.140 --> 01:08:39.840
I'm sorry.

1501
01:08:39.840 --> 01:08:40.840
I'm having a dream.

1502
01:08:40.880 --> 01:08:42.560
And I'm so sorry for anyone listening.

1503
01:08:42.920 --> 01:08:44.540
I probably then scared you.

1504
01:08:45.440 --> 01:08:53.220
What if one day we are doing Office Ladies and we get some soup delivered and it's from Brad Pitt?

1505
01:08:54.040 --> 01:08:54.920
Come on.

1506
01:08:55.160 --> 01:08:55.700
Could that happen?

1507
01:08:55.700 --> 01:08:56.400
And you know what?

1508
01:08:56.560 --> 01:08:57.760
Guess who's going to deliver it?

1509
01:08:58.360 --> 01:08:58.800
Keanu.

1510
01:09:00.420 --> 01:09:03.480
If Keanu Reeves delivered soup made by Brad Pitt.

1511
01:09:03.480 --> 01:09:10.740
And then all of a sudden, Idris Elba is going to, like, bring some music into it and we're going to just have, like, a soup-eating party.

1512
01:09:11.580 --> 01:09:12.900
What has just happened?

1513
01:09:13.000 --> 01:09:13.800
